 R←Test_API_039(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;tempDir;rc;msg;list;filename
⍝ Checks that Git does not escape non-ASCII characters in a path. With "core.quotepath" at its
⍝ default Git reports such a path octal-escaped and in double quotes, which turns a name like
⍝ "Cleanup_UC∆Stash1.aplf" into something no caller can use. <RunGitCommand> therefore passes
⍝ "-c core.quotepath=off" with every call.\\
⍝ The private copy has "core.quotepath" switched ON deliberately: that is what Git does without
⍝ a global setting, and it proves the command line wins over the repository configuration.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed

 tempDir←FilesAndDirs.GetTempSubDir'APLGit2-',⊃⎕SI
 (##.CiderConfig.HOME,'/TestData/CiderProject4.zip')ZipArchive.UnzipTo tempDir
 {}tempDir G.U.RunGitCommand'config core.quotepath true'
 filename←'APLSource/Counter∆1.aplf'
 (⊂' r←Counter∆1' ' r←1')⎕NPUT(tempDir,'/',filename)1

 list←0 1 G.Status tempDir
 →T.GoToTidyUp~(⊂filename)∊list[;3]

 R←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
 (rc msg)←FilesAndDirs.RmDirByForce tempDir
 msg Assert rc=0
⍝Done
